{"kind":"report","text":"Ready for independent exact-head review at clean head 7a4d4336239ba472f4df8c51220b699c40065e78 on task/status-fast-usable.\n\nThe branch first implemented the remaining combined status design, then integrated current main edb53cefddaaf2d06c75e2a53408c6104d27d206 without conflicts before publication. One internal statusview package now owns the MCP actor view and the global CLI/resident view. Default gs status is newest-first and bounds each actionable, attention, current-artifact, stale-artifact, and non-effective-attempt list at 20 with exact omitted counts; user text is a valid-UTF-8 240-byte maximum and fingerprints resolve to names without erasing unknown identities. Open unclaimed requests remain actionable without inventing a performer or waiting party. --all retains complete human tables and --json retains complete Snapshot JSON. The browser and /v0/status remain complete.\n\nAn explicit loopback --server uses /v0/status-summary under a two-second, 64 KiB, no-redirect client. The CLI validates genesis, head, depth/cursor consistency, and a stable local head before labeling the result resident-current. Redirecting, slow, oversized, foreign, stale, moving-head, malformed, or unavailable summaries are disclosed and select the signed-checkpoint local path. A local audit still running after one second prints one progress line. gs verify remains the unchanged full kernel audit.\n\nExact-head gates passed: make vet, make test, make race, make build; git diff --check; clean worktree; UI npm test (34/34) and npm run build after the current-main integration. Focused signed-checkpoint trust tests passed for restart/tail verification, profile/corruption/non-descendant fallback, envelope and cached-event guards, independent metadata binding, size enforcement, and wrong-sequencer rejection. Four build-valid mutations were applied and reverted: list cap 20→21, redirect refusal removed, genesis comparison removed, and summary response cap 64→128 KiB; each was killed by its named cap/trust test.\n\nMeasured at this exact head against the live depth-\u003e1000 workroom, three separate local checkpointed invocations were 1.88s, 0.21s, and 0.21s (median 0.21s); the slower first call printed the promised progress line. The previously approved checkpoint dependency's small-tail result remains 0.77s and its tail-bound tests are unchanged. The resident summary was 29,564 bytes and ten warm end-to-end CLI calls were 0.03s each. A synthetic projection with 10,000 entries in every growth dimension produced 21,978 bytes of JSON and 17,542 bytes of text while full text/JSON retained entries outside the window. One hundred loopback HTTP summary reads over a synthetic depth-20,000 projection measured 69.0ms p99, below 500ms.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:2b2cafd2580ade35d92701f2e1b0139b228410d8","branch":"task/status-fast-usable","head":"7a4d4336239ba472f4df8c51220b699c40065e78","status":"ready-for-review"}}